                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Looking back at 18 Wheels of Steel: Extreme Trucker, we can see that SCS Software always intended to create something as great as Euro Truck Simulator 2. For a game released in 2009, it was impressive, and any truck simulation fan can still enjoy it today.\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3777830984\nIn the past, they developed games under other publishers, which limited their creative freedom and kept them from adding the depth they wanted. However, once they began working independently, they delivered massive hits like ETS and ETS2. This game is clear proof that SCS was always ready to achieve great things.\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3777830915\nDriving on thin ice or navigating narrow mountain passes feels rewarding. While it may lack modern graphics, the variety of maps and distinctive atmosphere capture the true thrill of extreme driving.\n\n  [h1] a PEAK childhood game! [/h1]",
